Q9. Explain any five array methods.

Array methods are built-in JavaScript functions used to add, remove, or modify array elements.

1. push(): Adds one or more elements to the end of an array.
2. pop(): Removes the last element from an array.
3. shift(): Removes the first element from an array.
4. unshift(): Adds one or more elements to the beginning of an array.
5. map(): Creates a new array by applying a function to each element.

Example:

&#x20;   let numbers = [1, 2, 3];

numbers.push(4);     numbers.pop();

&#x20;   let result = numbers.map(n => n \* 2);

Q10. What is a callback method?

A callback is a function passed as an argument to another function so that it can be called later. Callbacks are commonly used in event handling and asynchronous operations.

Example:

function processNumber(number, callback)&#x20;

processNumber(5, function(value) );

In this example, the anonymous function is passed as a callback and executes when the processNumber() function calls it.
